content.text:
```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) p50_ms FROM (SELECT 'normal' p,* FROM normal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'abn',* FROM abnormal_traces) WHERE span_name IN ('geo.Geo/Nearby','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 2,3,4,1",
          "claim": "search's client span to geo.Geo/Nearby rises from p95 0.5ms to about 1642ms; geo's server span stays about 0.25ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH slow AS (SELECT trace_id FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND duration > 1e9 LIMIT 1) SELECT t.service_name, t.span_name, t.attr_span_kind, t.time, t.duration/1e6 ms FROM abnormal_traces t JOIN slow USING(trace_id) WHERE t.span_name IN ('geo.Geo/Nearby','search.Search/Nearby') ORDER BY t.time",
          "claim": "In a slow trace, search's geo client span starts about 1.6s before geo's server span, which lasts 0.26ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name IN ('rate.Rate/GetRates','geo.Geo/Nearby') GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "Only search's geo calls are slow in the abnormal period; its rate calls stay near 8.5ms p95."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p, span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'normal' p,* FROM normal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'abn',* FROM abnormal_traces) WHERE service_name='frontend' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 2,1",
          "claim": "Frontend's HTTP /hotels server p95 rises from 17.6ms to 1657ms, while other frontend endpoints stay flat."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The user-visible symptom is slow `/hotels` requests at the frontend (p95 17.6 ms → 1657 ms). The other frontend endpoints are unchanged. The chain is frontend `/hotels` → `search.Search/Nearby` → `geo.Geo/Nearby`. The delay of about 1.6 s sits in `search`'s outgoing call to `geo`, before `geo` handles the request. `geo`'s own server spans stay at about 0.25 ms. I classed it as `http_slow` at the caller because there were no network errors, retransmits or hubble per-connection metrics, and search's calls to `rate` on the same pod are unaffected. `network_delay` on the search–geo connection would also fit the timing, and I could not rule it out with this data.

I excluded the `rate` container CPU saturation (about 1.7 cores against about 0.006 normally). It is real, but `search → rate` latency did not change, so its effect did not reach users.

